.TH TG-EXEC 1 "October 2026" "tg-exec 2.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tg-exec \- run a command and report the result to Telegram
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tg-exec
[\fIoptions\fR]
.B \-\-
.I program
[\fIargs\fR...]
.br
.B tg-exec
[\fIoptions\fR]
.RI \(dq command\ line \(dq
.br
.B tg-exec
.BR \-\-setup " | " \-\-check " | " \-\-seal " | " \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tg-exec
runs a command, mirrors its output to the terminal and sends a Telegram
message when it finishes: status, exit code, duration, host and the tail of
the output. When the output does not fit into one message, the full log is
attached as a file. The exit code of the command is passed through, so
.B tg-exec
can wrap jobs in cron, systemd timers and CI without changing their result.
.PP
With several arguments (or after \fB\-\-\fR) the program is executed
directly and every argument is kept as is. With a single argument the string
is run by \fBbash \-c\fR (or \fB/bin/sh\fR), so pipes, redirections and
\fB&&\fR work.
.PP
A misconfigured notification never prevents the command from running: the
command is executed and the problem is reported on stderr.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-note " \fITEXT\fR"
Label shown in the message (default: host name).
.TP
.BI \-\-chat " ID"
Chat id: user, group (\-100...) or @channel.
.TP
.BI \-\-thread " ID"
Forum topic id in a supergroup with topics.
.TP
.BI \-\-notify " always|failure"
When to send a message. \fB\-\-on\-failure\fR is a shortcut for \fBfailure\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-output " always|failure|never"
When to include the command output.
.TP
.BI \-\-attach " auto|always|never"
Send the full output as a .log file: \fBauto\fR does it when the output does
not fit into the message (up to 45 MB).
.TP
.B \-\-silent
Deliver successful runs without sound.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-timeout " \fIDURATION\fR"
Stop the command after \fIDURATION\fR (90s, 30m, 2h): SIGTERM, then SIGKILL
after 10 seconds. Exit code 124.
.TP
.BI \-\-lang " ru|en"
Message language.
.TP
.BI \-\-proxy " URL"
\fBhttp://\fR, \fBhttps://\fR, \fBsocks5://\fR or \fBsocks5h://\fR proxy,
optionally with \fIuser:password@\fR; \fBnone\fR for a direct connection.
.TP
.BI \-\-config " FILE"
Additional config file with the highest file priority.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-shell
Join all arguments and run them via the shell.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Print the message to stderr instead of sending it.
.TP
.B \-\-strict
Exit with 70 if the command succeeded but the message could not be sent.
A failing command keeps its own exit code.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Diagnostics on stderr.
.TP
.B \-\-setup
Interactive setup: proxy, token check, chat discovery from recent messages to
the bot, label, language, test message. As root writes
\fI/etc/tg\-exec/config.conf\fR and offers to seal the token.
.TP
.B \-\-check
Print the effective settings with their sources, check the token and send a
silent test message.
.TP
.B \-\-seal
Encrypt the token with \fBsystemd\-creds\fR(1) into
\fI/etc/tg\-exec/token.cred\fR and replace \fBTOKEN\fR in the config with a
\fBTOKEN_CMD\fR that decrypts it. Requires root.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Settings are merged from (low to high priority):
\fI/etc/tg\-exec/config.conf\fR, \fI~/.config/tg\-exec/config.conf\fR
(\fI$XDG_CONFIG_HOME\fR), \fB\-\-config\fR, environment variables
\fBTG_EXEC_\fIKEY\fR, command-line options.
Files use \fBKEY="value"\fR lines; \fB$(hostname)\fR expands to the host name.
.TP
.BR TOKEN ", " TOKEN_FILE ", " TOKEN_CMD
Bot token, a file with it, or a command that prints it (like aws-cli
credential_process: \fBvault\fR, \fBpass\fR, \fBsystemd\-creds decrypt\fR).
The highest-priority source that sets any of the three wins. A systemd
credential named \fBtg\-exec\-token\fR (\fBLoadCredentialEncrypted=\fR) is used
first. \fBTELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN\fR is also accepted.
.TP
.BR CHAT_ID ", " THREAD_ID ", " NOTE
Destination and label. \fBTELEGRAM_CHAT_ID\fR is also accepted.
.TP
.BR NOTIFY ", " OUTPUT ", " ATTACH ", " SILENT_SUCCESS ", " LANG ", " TIMEZONE
Same as the options above. \fBALWAYS=1|0\fR (version 1) maps to
\fBOUTPUT=always|failure\fR.
.TP
.BR TIMEOUT ", " SHELL
Command timeout and the shell for single-string commands.
.TP
.BR PROXY ", " API_URL ", " CA_FILE
Proxy; own Bot API server or reverse proxy for closed networks; extra PEM CA
bundle. Without \fBPROXY\fR the standard \fBHTTPS_PROXY\fR, \fBALL_PROXY\fR
and \fBNO_PROXY\fR variables apply.
.TP
.BR HTTP_TIMEOUT ", " RETRIES ", " BACKOFF
Per-request timeout, total attempts (429 \fIretry_after\fR is respected),
first pause between attempts (doubles).
.TP
.BR STRICT ", " DEBUG
See \fB\-\-strict\fR and \fB\-\-debug\fR.
.SH SECURITY
A token that the program can read without a password can also be read by
whoever controls the account it runs as; encryption protects against stolen
disks and backups, not against root on a live host. Keep the config at mode
0600 (tg-exec warns otherwise), use a dedicated bot for notifications, and
prefer \fB\-\-seal\fR or \fBLoadCredentialEncrypted=\fR on servers.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The exit code of the command; 128+N if it was killed by signal N; 124 on
timeout; 127/126 if it could not be started; 70 with \fB\-\-strict\fR when a
successful run could not be reported; 2 on usage errors.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
tg\-exec \-\- apt\-get \-y upgrade
tg\-exec \-\-on\-failure "pg_dump app | gzip > /backup/app.sql.gz"
0 3 * * * tg\-exec \-n backup \-t 2h \-\- /usr/local/bin/backup.sh
TG_EXEC_PROXY=socks5h://127.0.0.1:1080 tg\-exec make release
.fi
.SH FILES
.I /etc/tg\-exec/config.conf
.br
.I ~/.config/tg\-exec/config.conf
.br
.I /etc/tg\-exec/token.cred
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemd\-creds (1),
.BR systemd.exec (5)
.PP
https://runstack.ru/p/tg\-exec
